# === Rust ===
# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# The dev-only oracle crates under `tooling/` are excluded from the workspace and built
# as path dev-dependencies via the root lockfile; a standalone `cargo build` inside one
# regenerates a redundant local lockfile that should not be committed.
tooling/*/Cargo.lock

# One deliberate exception. `tooling/c2pa-oracle` resolves a real external dependency tree
# (`c2pa`, the C2PA reference implementation) that no other manifest in this repository pins, so
# there is no root lockfile standing behind it: without one of its own, its whole transitive graph
# re-resolves on every invocation. Two things depend on that resolution being held still —
# `README.md` cites `c2pa`'s source **by line number**, and
# `tests/build_configuration.rs` asserts no OpenSSL package reached the graph. The exact `=`
# version pin in its manifest holds only the direct dependency; the assertion about the *graph*
# can otherwise only ever inspect the resolution cargo has just written, which is not an
# assertion. Committing this one lockfile is what makes it one.
!tooling/c2pa-oracle/Cargo.lock

# The fuzz tier's search state (issues #264, #311). The corpus is a search aid, not the regression
# record: a saved input is only reproducible while the target's byte-to-input mapping is unchanged,
# so a crash is minimised and promoted into a NAMED DETERMINISTIC TEST in the crate's own suite
# instead (see tooling/gamut-fuzz/README.md and docs/testing.md).
tooling/gamut-fuzz/artifacts/
tooling/gamut-fuzz/coverage/
# The persisted search corpus (#603): what the engine finds, kept apart from the curated seeds
# below so neither the Extended job's per-target cache nor a contributor's checkout can mix the
# two. The workflow passes `state/<target>/` as libFuzzer's first (written) corpus directory and
# `corpus/<target>/` as a read-only second one, and caches only the former.
tooling/gamut-fuzz/state/

# Everything under `corpus/` is ignored except the curated seed set, which is named file by file
# below. git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the ignore covers the
# directory's *contents* (`corpus/**`) and the per-target directories are re-opened (`!corpus/*/`)
# without re-including anything inside them. The seeds are then negated one path at a time — never
# by a wildcard: libFuzzer writes its findings into the same `corpus/<target>/` directory, and any
# pattern broad enough to cover a future seed would cover those too. Adding a seed is one line here
# plus a plain `git add` (see "Seeds" in tooling/gamut-fuzz/README.md).
tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/**
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/*/
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/avif_clean_alpha/16bit-1x3-edge.bin
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/avif_clean_alpha/8bit-2x2-edge.bin
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/avif_parse_decode/grid-2x2-limits-6.avif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/avif_parse_decode/overlay-two-inputs-limits-100px.avif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/dng_decode/cfa-12bit.dng
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/heic_container/appended-stream.heic
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/heic_container/heic-single-item.heic
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/heic_container/trailer.heic
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/heic_hvcc/main-still-vps-sps-pps.bin
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/heic_hvcc/truncated-payload-nal.bin
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/01-truncated-header.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/03-invalid-byte-order.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/04-invalid-magic.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/05-ifd0-offset-past-eof.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/06-truncated-entry-count.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/07-truncated-entries.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/08-value-offset-past-eof.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/09a-circular-ifd-self.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/09b-circular-ifd-two-node.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/10a-hostile-entry-count.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/10b-hostile-entry-count-bigtiff.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/11-hostile-value-count.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/12-unknown-tag-preserved.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/13-unknown-field-type.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/ifd_read/padding-unread-claim.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/isobmff_boxes/avif-single-item.avif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/tiff_decode/rgb8-lzw.tif
!tooling/gamut-fuzz/corpus/tiff_decode/rgb8-none.tif

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Coverage artifacts
lcov.info

# hk (git hook runner): per-developer, uncommitted hook overrides
hk.local.pkl

